@intology reports that Codex, Claude Code, and Autoresearch recover only 9.3% of human progress, mainly focusing on hyperparameter tuning and rarely attempting algorithmic research. Although Claude Code and Autoresearch reason more about algorithms, they still avoid implementation.

NanoGPT-Bench is an autonomous, end-to-end evaluation built on the NanoGPT Speedrun, a popular competition aiming to minimize GPT-2 style model training time. It standardizes evaluation to a 5-month window of world records, representing nearly 2 years of human effort, with no human intervention or internet access.

