Another notable open-source release is Miso One, an 8-billion-parameter text-to-speech model capable of expressing a wide range of emotions. It generates speech with warmth, hesitation, and excitement, making voiceovers more natural and engaging. Designed for applications like shorts, podcasts, and educational content, it operates with a latency of 110 milliseconds, faster than human reaction time. The model weights are fully open source, allowing users to clone, self-host, fine-tune, and keep their data private.

@AodenTeoMT: "Today, we’re excited to introduce Miso One, the most emotive voice model in the world. Miso One is an 8-billion-parameter text-to-speech model for highly expressive speech generation. It emotes like a human and responds faster than a human, with just 110 milliseconds of latency. We’ve open-sourced the model weights, with API access coming soon. Hear how Miso One sounds in the thread below."

The model is available on GitHub, where it is described as a highly emotive TTS system that can generate expressive speech responses.

